IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g7-interpretation`

-- g7-vintages: the amending history of the Law as DATA (endnotes: Table of Legislation History rows for the eight amending instruments, Table of Endnote
-- References notes [1], [2] and [5]) and the resolver from a day, or from an instant, to a `Vintage of the text` of domain.l4 (integration point IP2).
--
-- What the sources show and what they do not (every claim below was read in inputs/amending/ on 2026-10-26):
--   * R&O.40/2019, R&O.29/2021, R&O.28/2023, R&O.10/2024 and R&O.102/2026 each state the day or the time they come into force; the three Orders that come into
--     force "7 days after it is made" (R&O.28/2023 Article 3, R&O.56/2025 Article 2, R&O.102/2026 Article 7(6)) name the day they were made.
--   * L.13/2019 Schedule 3 paragraph 1 amends Article 1 "Comptroller"; R&O.136/2019 Article 1 brings that Law into force on 1 January 2020 except its Articles 17 to 19,
--     so the Schedule is in force from that day: the Table (src:890-893) and the Appointed Day Act agree.
--   * L.1/2017 Article 30(3) adds the two "subject to Article 20(1) of the Dormant Bank Accounts (Jersey) Law 2017" openings to Schedule 1; its Article 31(2) leaves the day to
--     an Act of the States.  The Act that appointed 16 December 2019 is NOT among the sources: that date rests on the Table alone.
--   * R&O.29/2021 changes the Charities Law nowhere but in Schedule 2 paragraph 1(e) (the definition of "Minister" in Article 1).
--   * No text of the Law before 1 January 2019 is among the nine versions; the days before it answer `before the first consolidated version`.
--   * The text of the definition of "Minister" in force from 1 January 2019 to 30 May 2019 is INFERRED: R&O.40/2019 Schedule 2 paragraph 1(e) substitutes
--     "Minister for External Relations" for "Chief Minister", which shows the words it replaced; endnote [1] lists no earlier amendment of Article 1.
--   * Time of day: only R&O.10/2024 states one (9.30 a.m. on 27 February 2024).  Jersey time is taken as the tz database zone Europe/Jersey (assumed, not ruled).
--
-- A vintage that does not decide a fact answers REFUSE, never a value borrowed from a neighbour.  Nothing here gates another group's rule: the integrator
-- wraps the headline exports of the other groups.

§ `Endnotes`

§§ `The time zone and the shape of the data`

-- Assumed, not ruled: the dates and the 9.30 a.m. of the instruments are Jersey local time.
@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Endnotes, Table of Legislation History, R&O.10/2024, “9.30 a.m. on 27 February 2024” (src:903-906)
GIVETH A STRING
`the time zone in which the dates of the Law are stated` MEANS "Europe/Jersey"

-- How an instrument fixes the moment it comes into force.  Only R&O.10/2024 states a time of day.
DECLARE `How an instrument comes into force` IS ONE OF
    `on a day stated` HAS day IS A DATE @desc The first day on which the instrument is in force, as the instrument or the Table states it
    `at a stated time on a day` HAS day IS A DATE @desc The day
                                    hour IS A NUMBER @desc The hour, 0 to 23, Jersey time
                                    minute IS A NUMBER @desc The minute, 0 to 59
    `a number of days after it is made` HAS days IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days after the day of making (7 in the three Orders that use this form)

-- One amending instrument of the Table of Legislation History, with what the sources show of it.
DECLARE `Amending instrument` HAS
    identifier IS A STRING @desc The identifier the Table uses, for example R&O.40/2019
    title IS A STRING @desc The title of the instrument
    `made on` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc The day it was made; NOTHING where the sources do not show a day on which it was made
    `comes into force` IS A `How an instrument comes into force` @desc How the instrument fixes the moment it comes into force
    `what it does to the Law` IS A STRING @desc The change it makes to the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014
    `text among the sources` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the text of the instrument is among the sources of this encoding
    `date in force shown by the sources` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an instrument among the sources states the day it comes into force, and not only the Table

-- One text of the Law: the version that takes effect with an instrument (or with the remainder of the Law itself, for the first version).
DECLARE `Text of the Law` HAS
    vintage IS A `Vintage of the text` @desc The version of the consolidated text
    `brought by` IS A MAYBE `Amending instrument` @desc The amending instrument that made this version; NOTHING for the first version, which is the Law as it stood when the remainder came into force
    `takes effect` IS A `How an instrument comes into force` @desc How the version takes effect

-- Which enactment the definition of "Comptroller" in Article 1 points at.  Group-local: domain.l4 has no such noun (nouns request in FRAGMENT-G7.md).
DECLARE `Enactment that defines the Comptroller` IS ONE OF
    `the Income Tax (Jersey) Law 1961`
    `the Revenue Administration (Jersey) Law 2019`

§§ `Named refusals`

-- A refusal is returned, never stored (phrasebook 11.8): each is a definition at any type whose name is its message.
@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Endnotes, Table of Legislation History, row L.41/2014, “Remainder in force 1 January 2019” (src:880)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the text of the Law before 1 January 2019 is not among the nine versions in the sources` MEANS
    REFUSE "the text of the Law before 1 January 2019 is not among the nine versions in the sources"

@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Endnotes, Table of Legislation History, R&O.10/2024 (src:903-906)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the text of the Law changes partway through this day, so a question about the day alone has no answer` MEANS
    REFUSE "the text of the Law changes partway through this day (9.30 a.m. on 27 February 2024, R&O.10/2024), so a question about the day alone has no answer: ask about an instant, or choose the other reading of F7.1"

@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Endnotes, Table of Legislation History (src:876-912)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the sources do not show the day on which this instrument was made` MEANS
    REFUSE "the sources do not show the day on which this instrument was made, and it comes into force a number of days after it is made"

§§ `Table of Legislation History: the eight amending instruments (rows E4 to E11)`

-- Row E4.  R&O.40/2019 states: Made 31st May 2019, Coming into force 31st May 2019.  Its Schedule 2 paragraph 1(e) is the one that reaches this Law.
-- src:882 | States of Jersey (Transfer of Responsibilities and
-- src:883 | Functions) (Chief Minister to External Relations) Order 2019
-- src:884 | R&O.40/2019
-- src:885 | 31 May 2019
@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Endnotes, Table of Legislation History, R&O.40/2019 (src:882-885)
GIVETH AN `Amending instrument`
`R&O.40/2019` MEANS
    `Amending instrument` WITH
        identifier IS "R&O.40/2019"
        title IS "States of Jersey (Transfer of Responsibilities and Functions) (Chief Minister to External Relations) Order 2019"
        `made on` IS JUST (YMD 2019 5 31)
        `comes into force` IS `on a day stated` (YMD 2019 5 31)
        `what it does to the Law` IS "Article 1, definition of “Minister”: for “Chief Minister” there is substituted “Minister for External Relations” (Schedule 2 paragraph 1(e))"
        `text among the sources` IS TRUE
        `date in force shown by the sources` IS TRUE

-- Row E5.  L.1/2017 Article 30(3) adds the Dormant Bank Accounts openings to Schedule 1 paragraphs 2(4)(a) and 4(7).  Its Article 31(2) leaves the day to an Act of the
-- States, which is not among the sources: the day rests on the Table alone (trap T22).  The day it was made is not shown (it was adopted on 28 June 2016 and registered on
-- 24 February 2017; neither is the day the amendment was made).
-- src:886 | Dormant Bank Accounts (Jersey) Law 2017
-- src:887 | L.1/2017
-- src:888 | 16 December 2019
-- src:889 | P.25/2016
