§§ `When each instrument comes into force (the counting conventions F7.1, F7.2 and F7.11)`

-- F7.11.  The Table names the day on which an instrument comes into force; the reading taken is that the named day is the FIRST day in force (R&O.17/2018 Article 1:
-- "come into force on 1st May 2018"; the three Orders that come into force "7 days after it is made" reach the Table's dates on this reading, F7.2).
-- The other reading makes the day after the named day the first day in force.
@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Endnotes, Table of Legislation History (src:876-912)
GIVEN named IS A DATE @desc The day the instrument or the Table names as the day of commencement
      interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes` @desc The reading chosen at each fork; this function reads F7.11
GIVETH A DATE
`the first day in force of a commencement that names the day` named interp MEANS
    CONSIDER interp's `how the day named as the day of commencement is counted`
    WHEN `the named day is the first day in force` THEN named
    WHEN `the day after the named day is the first day in force` THEN Date (Day named PLUS 1)

-- F7.2.  "comes into force 7 days after it is made" (R&O.28/2023 Article 3, R&O.56/2025 Article 2, R&O.102/2026 Article 7(6)).  The reading taken leaves the day of making out
-- and counts the seventh day after it as the first day in force: 5 April + 7 = 12 April 2023; 9 October + 7 = 16 October 2025; 25 September + 7 = 2 October 2026, each the date the
-- Table gives.  The other reading leaves seven clear days after the day of making, so the eighth day after it is the first day in force; the Table's dates refute it.
@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Endnotes, Table of Legislation History, R&O.28/2023, R&O.56/2025, R&O.102/2026 (src:899-902), (src:907-912)
GIVEN count IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days after the day of making
      made IS A DATE @desc The day the instrument was made
      interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes` @desc The reading chosen at each fork; this function reads F7.2
GIVETH A DATE
`the first day in force a number of days after the day of making` count made interp MEANS
    CONSIDER interp's `how “7 days after it is made” is counted`
    WHEN `the day of making is left out` THEN Date (Day made PLUS count)
    WHEN `seven clear days are left` THEN Date (Day made PLUS count PLUS 1)

@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Endnotes, Table of Legislation History, R&O.28/2023, R&O.56/2025, R&O.102/2026 (src:899-902), (src:907-912)
@export The day on which an instrument made on a given day and coming into force “7 days after it is made” comes into force, on the reading chosen at F7.2 (default: the seventh day after the day of making)
GIVEN made IS A DATE @desc The day the instrument was made, for example 2025-10-09
      interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes` @desc The reading chosen at each fork; this function reads F7.2
GIVETH A DATE
`Endnotes: the day an instrument made on a day comes into force 7 days after` made interp MEANS
    `the first day in force a number of days after the day of making` 7 made interp

-- The first day on which an instrument is in force (its day, whatever the hour).
@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Endnotes, Table of Legislation History (src:876-912)
GIVEN how IS A `How an instrument comes into force`
      made IS A MAYBE DATE
      interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes`
GIVETH A DATE
`the first day on which a commencement is in force` how made interp MEANS
    CONSIDER how
    WHEN `on a day stated` d THEN `the first day in force of a commencement that names the day` d interp
    WHEN `at a stated time on a day` d h m THEN d
    WHEN `a number of days after it is made` n THEN
        CONSIDER made
        WHEN JUST m THEN `the first day in force a number of days after the day of making` n m interp
        WHEN NOTHING THEN `the sources do not show the day on which this instrument was made`

-- The instant at which a commencement takes effect: the start of its first day in force (Jersey time), or the stated time.
@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Endnotes, Table of Legislation History (src:876-912)
GIVEN how IS A `How an instrument comes into force`
      made IS A MAYBE DATE
      interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes`
GIVETH A DATETIME
`the instant at which a commencement takes effect` how made interp MEANS
    CONSIDER how
    WHEN `at a stated time on a day` d h m THEN
        DATETIME_FROM_DTZ d (TIME_FROM_HMS h m 0) `the time zone in which the dates of the Law are stated`
    OTHERWISE
        DATETIME_FROM_DTZ (`the first day on which a commencement is in force` how made interp) (TIME_FROM_HMS 0 0 0) `the time zone in which the dates of the Law are stated`

-- Whether a commencement takes effect partway through its day (it states a time of day).
@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Endnotes, Table of Legislation History (src:876-912)
GIVEN how IS A `How an instrument comes into force`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a commencement takes effect partway through its day` how MEANS
    CONSIDER how
    WHEN `at a stated time on a day` d h m THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `Table of Legislation History: the nine texts of the Law`

-- The nine point-in-time versions of the consolidated text, in order.  The first is the Law as it stood when the remainder came into force on 1 January 2019
-- (R&O.17/2018 Article 2, row E3); each of the other eight is made by one amending instrument.  Which instrument made which text is read from the Table.
-- src:876 | Parts 1 to 3, Articles 32, 38, 39, 40, 42, 43 and 44 and
-- src:877 | the Schedules, in force 21 November 2014;
-- src:878 | Parts 4, 5, 7, 8 (other than Article 32), Article 37 in
-- src:879 | force 1 May 2018 (R&O.17/2018);
-- src:880 | Remainder in force 1 January 2019 (R&O.17/2018).
@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Endnotes, Table of Legislation History, row L.41/2014, “Remainder in force 1 January 2019 (R&O.17/2018)” (src:880)
GIVETH A `Text of the Law`
`the text of the Law that took effect with the remainder` MEANS
    `Text of the Law` WITH
        vintage IS `the text of 1 January 2019`
        `brought by` IS NOTHING
        `takes effect` IS `on a day stated` (YMD 2019 1 1)

@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Endnotes, Table of Legislation History, R&O.40/2019 (src:882-885)
GIVETH A `Text of the Law`
`the text of the Law that took effect with R&O.40/2019` MEANS
    `Text of the Law` WITH
        vintage IS `the text of 31 May 2019`
        `brought by` IS JUST `R&O.40/2019`
        `takes effect` IS `R&O.40/2019`'s `comes into force`

@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Endnotes, Table of Legislation History, L.1/2017 (src:886-889)
GIVETH A `Text of the Law`
`the text of the Law that took effect with L.1/2017` MEANS
    `Text of the Law` WITH
        vintage IS `the text of 16 December 2019`
        `brought by` IS JUST `L.1/2017`
        `takes effect` IS `L.1/2017`'s `comes into force`

@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Endnotes, Table of Legislation History, L.13/2019 (src:890-893)
GIVETH A `Text of the Law`
`the text of the Law that took effect with L.13/2019` MEANS
    `Text of the Law` WITH
        vintage IS `the text of 1 January 2020`
        `brought by` IS JUST `L.13/2019`
        `takes effect` IS `L.13/2019`'s `comes into force`

@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Endnotes, Table of Legislation History, R&O.29/2021 (src:894-898)
GIVETH A `Text of the Law`
`the text of the Law that took effect with R&O.29/2021` MEANS
    `Text of the Law` WITH
        vintage IS `the text of 2 March 2021`
        `brought by` IS JUST `R&O.29/2021`
        `takes effect` IS `R&O.29/2021`'s `comes into force`

@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Endnotes, Table of Legislation History, R&O.28/2023 (src:899-902)
GIVETH A `Text of the Law`
`the text of the Law that took effect with R&O.28/2023` MEANS
    `Text of the Law` WITH
        vintage IS `the text of 12 April 2023`
        `brought by` IS JUST `R&O.28/2023`
        `takes effect` IS `R&O.28/2023`'s `comes into force`

@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Endnotes, Table of Legislation History, R&O.10/2024 (src:903-906)
GIVETH A `Text of the Law`
`the text of the Law that took effect with R&O.10/2024` MEANS
    `Text of the Law` WITH
        vintage IS `the text of 27 February 2024`
        `brought by` IS JUST `R&O.10/2024`
        `takes effect` IS `R&O.10/2024`'s `comes into force`

@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Endnotes, Table of Legislation History, R&O.56/2025 (src:907-909)
GIVETH A `Text of the Law`
`the text of the Law that took effect with R&O.56/2025` MEANS
    `Text of the Law` WITH
        vintage IS `the text of 16 October 2025`
        `brought by` IS JUST `R&O.56/2025`
        `takes effect` IS `R&O.56/2025`'s `comes into force`

@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Endnotes, Table of Legislation History, R&O.102/2026 (src:910-912)
GIVETH A `Text of the Law`
`the text of the Law that took effect with R&O.102/2026` MEANS
    `Text of the Law` WITH
        vintage IS `the text of 2 October 2026`
        `brought by` IS JUST `R&O.102/2026`
        `takes effect` IS `R&O.102/2026`'s `comes into force`

-- The nine texts, in order.
@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Endnotes, Table of Legislation History (src:876-912)
GIVETH A LIST OF `Text of the Law`
`the nine texts of the Law` MEANS
    LIST `the text of the Law that took effect with the remainder`,
         `the text of the Law that took effect with R&O.40/2019`,
         `the text of the Law that took effect with L.1/2017`,
         `the text of the Law that took effect with L.13/2019`,
         `the text of the Law that took effect with R&O.29/2021`,
         `the text of the Law that took effect with R&O.28/2023`,
         `the text of the Law that took effect with R&O.10/2024`,
         `the text of the Law that took effect with R&O.56/2025`,
         `the text of the Law that took effect with R&O.102/2026`

§§ `The resolver: which text is in force`

-- The instant at which a text takes effect.
@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Endnotes, Table of Legislation History (src:876-912)
GIVEN row IS A `Text of the Law`
      interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes`
GIVETH A DATETIME
`the instant at which a text of the Law takes effect` row interp MEANS
    `the instant at which a commencement takes effect` (row's `takes effect`) (`the day the instrument that brought a text was made` row) interp

@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Endnotes, Table of Legislation History (src:876-912)
GIVEN row IS A `Text of the Law`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the day the instrument that brought a text was made` row MEANS
    CONSIDER row's `brought by`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST instrument THEN instrument's `made on`

-- Order of two instants.  The `datetime` library defines the comparison operators on DATETIME, but a group module may import only prelude, daydate, domain and its own group
-- (brief, ruling 1), so the instants are compared by their serial numbers (days since the epoch of L4, with the fraction of the day), which DATETIME_SERIAL gives in UTC.
@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Endnotes, Table of Legislation History (src:876-912)
GIVEN earlier IS A DATETIME
      later IS A DATETIME
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the endnote instant` earlier `is not later than the endnote instant` later MEANS
    DATETIME_SERIAL earlier AT MOST DATETIME_SERIAL later

-- The latest version of a chronological list.
@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Endnotes, Table of Legislation History (src:876-912)
GIVEN found IS A LIST OF `Vintage of the text`
GIVETH A `Vintage of the text`
`the latest of these versions of the text` found MEANS
    CONSIDER reverse found
    WHEN EMPTY THEN `before the first consolidated version`
    WHEN latest FOLLOWED BY earlier THEN latest

-- The text in force at an instant: the latest version that has taken effect by then.  Before the first, `before the first consolidated version`.
@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Endnotes, Table of Legislation History (src:876-912)
@export The version of the consolidated text of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 in force at a given instant (one of the nine versions, or "before the first consolidated version" for an instant before 1 January 2019)
GIVEN `the moment` IS A DATETIME @desc The moment asked about, with its time zone, for example 2024-02-27T09:30:00Z
      interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes` @desc The reading chosen at each fork; this function reads F7.2 and F7.11
GIVETH A `Vintage of the text`
`Endnotes: the vintage of the text at` `the moment` interp MEANS
    `the latest of these versions of the text`
        (map (GIVEN row YIELD row's vintage)
             (filter (GIVEN row YIELD `the endnote instant` (`the instant at which a text of the Law takes effect` row interp) `is not later than the endnote instant` `the moment`)
                     `the nine texts of the Law`))

-- The start of a day, Jersey time, as an instant.
@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Endnotes, Table of Legislation History (src:876-912)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATETIME
`the start of a day of the Law in Jersey time` d MEANS
    DATETIME_FROM_DTZ d (TIME_FROM_HMS 0 0 0) `the time zone in which the dates of the Law are stated`

@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Endnotes, Table of Legislation History (src:876-912)
GIVEN earlier IS A DATETIME
      later IS A DATETIME
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the endnote instant` earlier `is earlier than the endnote instant` later MEANS
    DATETIME_SERIAL earlier LESS THAN DATETIME_SERIAL later

-- The texts that have taken effect by the start of a day.
@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Endnotes, Table of Legislation History (src:876-912)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Text of the Law`
`the texts that have taken effect by the start of` d interp MEANS
    filter (GIVEN row YIELD `the endnote instant` (`the instant at which a text of the Law takes effect` row interp) `is not later than the endnote instant` (`the start of a day of the Law in Jersey time` d))
           `the nine texts of the Law`

-- The texts that take effect during a day, after its start (a text that takes effect at the very start of the day is not among them).
@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Endnotes, Table of Legislation History (src:876-912)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Text of the Law`
`the texts that take effect during` d interp MEANS
    filter (GIVEN row YIELD
                    `the endnote instant` (`the start of a day of the Law in Jersey time` d) `is earlier than the endnote instant` (`the instant at which a text of the Law takes effect` row interp)
                AND `the endnote instant` (`the instant at which a text of the Law takes effect` row interp) `is earlier than the endnote instant` (`the start of a day of the Law in Jersey time` (Date (Day d PLUS 1))))
           `the nine texts of the Law`

-- Every version that is in force at some moment of a day: the one in force at its start, then each that takes effect during it.
-- F7.1.  On an ordinary day there is one version.  On a day on which a text takes effect at a stated time (27 February 2024, R&O.10/2024) there are two on the reading taken,
-- so a question about the day alone cannot be answered unless both versions give the same answer; the other reading puts the whole day in the new text, which leaves one.
@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Endnotes, Table of Legislation History (src:876-912)
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
      interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Vintage of the text`
`the versions in force at some moment of` `the day` interp MEANS
    (`the latest of these versions of the text` (map (GIVEN row YIELD row's vintage) (`the texts that have taken effect by the start of` `the day` interp)))
        FOLLOWED BY (map (GIVEN row YIELD row's vintage) (`the texts that take effect during` `the day` interp))

@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Endnotes, Table of Legislation History (src:876-912)
@export The versions of the consolidated text of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 that are in force on a given day, as the reading chosen at F7.1 counts them: one version on an ordinary day; on 27 February 2024 two (the text changes at 9.30 a.m.) on the reading taken, one on the other reading
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day asked about, for example 2024-02-27
      interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes` @desc The reading chosen at each fork; this function reads F7.1 (and F7.2, F7.11)
GIVETH A LIST OF `Vintage of the text`
`Endnotes: the texts in force at some time on` `the day` interp MEANS
    CONSIDER interp's `how a day on which a text takes effect at a stated time is treated`
    WHEN `a question about that day alone is refused` THEN `the versions in force at some moment of` `the day` interp
    WHEN `the whole day is in the new text` THEN LIST (`the latest of these versions of the text` (`the versions in force at some moment of` `the day` interp))

-- F7.1.  The version in force on a day: the one version, or a refusal where the day has two (the reading taken refuses a question about 27 February 2024 alone and answers a question
-- about an instant; the other reading, which has one version for that day, answers it).
@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Endnotes, Table of Legislation History (src:876-912)
@export The version of the consolidated text of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 in force on a given day: one of the nine versions, "before the first consolidated version" for a day before 1 January 2019, and a refusal for 27 February 2024 on the reading taken at F7.1 (the text changes at 9.30 a.m.; ask about an instant)
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day asked about, for example 2026-10-02
      interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes` @desc The reading chosen at each fork; this function reads F7.1 (and F7.2, F7.11)
GIVETH A `Vintage of the text`
`Endnotes: the vintage of the text on` `the day` interp MEANS
    CONSIDER `Endnotes: the texts in force at some time on` `the day` interp
    WHEN EMPTY THEN `before the first consolidated version`
    WHEN only FOLLOWED BY EMPTY THEN only
    WHEN first FOLLOWED BY later THEN `the text of the Law changes partway through this day, so a question about the day alone has no answer`

§§ `What each version says (the facts the other groups read)`

-- Article 1, definition of "Minister": the office named, text by text.  The first text (1 January 2019 to 30 May 2019) is INFERRED: R&O.40/2019 Schedule 2 paragraph 1(e) substitutes
-- “Minister for External Relations” for “Chief Minister”, which shows the words it replaced, and endnote [1] lists no amendment of Article 1 before it.  For a day before 1 January 2019 the
-- sources show no text of the Law at all.
-- src:26 | “Minister” means the Chief Minister;
@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Article 1, definition of “Minister”, as amended (src:26)
@export The office that the definition of “Minister” in Article 1 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 names in a given version of the text; refuses for the days before 1 January 2019
GIVEN `the vintage of the text` IS A `Vintage of the text` @desc One of the nine versions of the consolidated text, or "before the first consolidated version"
GIVETH AN `Office of the Minister`
`Endnotes: the office that the definition of “Minister” names under the text of` `the vintage of the text` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the vintage of the text`
    WHEN `before the first consolidated version` THEN `the text of the Law before 1 January 2019 is not among the nine versions in the sources`
    WHEN `the text of 1 January 2019` THEN `the Chief Minister`
    WHEN `the text of 31 May 2019` THEN `the Minister for External Relations`
    WHEN `the text of 16 December 2019` THEN `the Minister for External Relations`
    WHEN `the text of 1 January 2020` THEN `the Minister for External Relations`
    WHEN `the text of 2 March 2021` THEN `the Minister for External Relations and Financial Services`
    WHEN `the text of 12 April 2023` THEN `the Chief Minister`
    WHEN `the text of 27 February 2024` THEN `the Minister for External Relations`
    WHEN `the text of 16 October 2025` THEN `the Minister for External Relations`
    WHEN `the text of 2 October 2026` THEN `the Chief Minister`

-- Article 1, definition of "Comptroller": the Law it points at, text by text.  Before 1 January 2020 the Income Tax (Jersey) Law 1961; from that day the Revenue Administration (Jersey) Law 2019
-- (L.13/2019 Schedule 3 paragraph 1, in force with that Law on 1 January 2020 by R&O.136/2019 Article 1).
-- src:12 | “Comptroller” has the meaning given by the Revenue Administration (Jersey) Law 2019;
@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Article 1, definition of “Comptroller”, as amended (src:12)
@export The enactment that the definition of “Comptroller” in Article 1 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 points at in a given version of the text; refuses for the days before 1 January 2019
GIVEN `the vintage of the text` IS A `Vintage of the text` @desc One of the nine versions of the consolidated text, or "before the first consolidated version"
GIVETH AN `Enactment that defines the Comptroller`
`Endnotes: the enactment that defines the Comptroller under the text of` `the vintage of the text` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the vintage of the text`
    WHEN `before the first consolidated version` THEN `the text of the Law before 1 January 2019 is not among the nine versions in the sources`
    WHEN `the text of 1 January 2019` THEN `the Income Tax (Jersey) Law 1961`
    WHEN `the text of 31 May 2019` THEN `the Income Tax (Jersey) Law 1961`
    WHEN `the text of 16 December 2019` THEN `the Income Tax (Jersey) Law 1961`
    WHEN `the text of 1 January 2020` THEN `the Revenue Administration (Jersey) Law 2019`
    WHEN `the text of 2 March 2021` THEN `the Revenue Administration (Jersey) Law 2019`
    WHEN `the text of 12 April 2023` THEN `the Revenue Administration (Jersey) Law 2019`
    WHEN `the text of 27 February 2024` THEN `the Revenue Administration (Jersey) Law 2019`
    WHEN `the text of 16 October 2025` THEN `the Revenue Administration (Jersey) Law 2019`
    WHEN `the text of 2 October 2026` THEN `the Revenue Administration (Jersey) Law 2019`

-- Article 2(1)(ba): inserted by R&O.56/2025 (in force 16 October 2025); in the texts from that day only.
-- src:51 | (ba) a body corporate that –
-- src:52 | (i) is an NPO, as defined by the Non-Profit Organizations (Jersey) Law 2008;
-- src:53 | (ii) is established under the law of Jersey; and
-- src:54 | (iii) does not fall within any of sub-paragraphs (c) to (h);
@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Article 2(1)(ba), inserted by R&O.56/2025 (src:51-54)
@export Whether paragraph (ba) of Article 2(1) of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 (a body corporate that is an NPO established under the law of Jersey) is in a given version of the text; refuses for the days before 1 January 2019
GIVEN `the vintage of the text` IS A `Vintage of the text` @desc One of the nine versions of the consolidated text, or "before the first consolidated version"
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Endnotes: Article 2(1)(ba) is in the text of` `the vintage of the text` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the vintage of the text`
    WHEN `before the first consolidated version` THEN `the text of the Law before 1 January 2019 is not among the nine versions in the sources`
    WHEN `the text of 1 January 2019` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the text of 31 May 2019` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the text of 16 December 2019` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the text of 1 January 2020` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the text of 2 March 2021` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the text of 12 April 2023` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the text of 27 February 2024` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the text of 16 October 2025` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the text of 2 October 2026` THEN TRUE

-- Schedule 1 paragraphs 2(4)(a) and 4(7): the two openings "subject to Article 20(1) of the Dormant Bank Accounts (Jersey) Law 2017", added by L.1/2017 Article 30(3) from 16 December 2019 (the Table).
-- src:776 | (a) subject to Article 20(1) of the Dormant Bank Accounts (Jersey) Law 2017, the remuneration or other payment for services of the Commissioner, due under the terms of his or her appointment, must be paid out of the annual income of the States; and
-- src:806 | (7) Subject to Article 20(1) of the Dormant Bank Accounts (Jersey) Law 2017, the cost of providing staff, accommodation and equipment under this paragraph must be met out of the annual income of the States.
@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Schedule 1 paragraphs 2(4)(a) and 4(7), as amended by L.1/2017 Article 30(3) (src:776)
@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Schedule 1 paragraph 4(7), as amended by L.1/2017 Article 30(3) (src:806)
@export Whether the two openings “subject to Article 20(1) of the Dormant Bank Accounts (Jersey) Law 2017” of Schedule 1 paragraphs 2(4)(a) and 4(7) of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 are in a given version of the text; refuses for the days before 1 January 2019
GIVEN `the vintage of the text` IS A `Vintage of the text` @desc One of the nine versions of the consolidated text, or "before the first consolidated version"
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Endnotes: the Dormant Bank Accounts openings of Schedule 1 are in the text of` `the vintage of the text` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the vintage of the text`
    WHEN `before the first consolidated version` THEN `the text of the Law before 1 January 2019 is not among the nine versions in the sources`
    WHEN `the text of 1 January 2019` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the text of 31 May 2019` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the text of 16 December 2019` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the text of 1 January 2020` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the text of 2 March 2021` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the text of 12 April 2023` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the text of 27 February 2024` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the text of 16 October 2025` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the text of 2 October 2026` THEN TRUE

§§ `The same facts asked of a day or of an instant`

-- A day on which two versions are in force answers only where both versions give the same answer; otherwise it refuses.  (Reading B of F7.1 leaves one version.)
@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Endnotes, Table of Legislation History (src:876-912)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the versions in force during this day disagree, so a question about the day alone has no answer` MEANS
    REFUSE "the versions in force at different moments of this day disagree on this fact (27 February 2024, R&O.10/2024: the text changes at 9.30 a.m.), so a question about the day alone has no answer: ask about an instant"

@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Endnotes, Table of Legislation History (src:876-912)
GIVEN offices IS A LIST OF `Office of the Minister`
GIVETH AN `Office of the Minister`
`the office on which the versions agree` offices MEANS
    CONSIDER offices
    WHEN EMPTY THEN `the text of the Law before 1 January 2019 is not among the nine versions in the sources`
    WHEN first FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        IF all (GIVEN other YIELD other EQUALS first) rest
        THEN first
        ELSE `the versions in force during this day disagree, so a question about the day alone has no answer`

@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Endnotes, Table of Legislation History (src:876-912)
GIVEN enactments IS A LIST OF `Enactment that defines the Comptroller`
GIVETH AN `Enactment that defines the Comptroller`
`the enactment on which the versions agree` enactments MEANS
    CONSIDER enactments
    WHEN EMPTY THEN `the text of the Law before 1 January 2019 is not among the nine versions in the sources`
    WHEN first FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        IF all (GIVEN other YIELD other EQUALS first) rest
        THEN first
        ELSE `the versions in force during this day disagree, so a question about the day alone has no answer`

@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Endnotes, Table of Legislation History (src:876-912)
GIVEN answers IS A LIST OF BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the answer on which the versions agree` answers MEANS
    BRANCH IF null answers THEN `the text of the Law before 1 January 2019 is not among the nine versions in the sources`
           IF all (GIVEN a YIELD a) answers THEN TRUE
           IF all (GIVEN a YIELD NOT a) answers THEN FALSE
           OTHERWISE `the versions in force during this day disagree, so a question about the day alone has no answer`

@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Article 1, definition of “Minister”, as amended; Endnotes, Table of Legislation History (src:26), (src:876-912)
@export The office that the definition of “Minister” in Article 1 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 names on a given day; refuses before 1 January 2019, and on 27 February 2024 (the office changes at 9.30 a.m.) on the reading taken at F7.1
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day asked about, for example 2024-02-26
      interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes` @desc The reading chosen at each fork; this function reads F7.1
GIVETH AN `Office of the Minister`
`Endnotes: the office of the Minister on` `the day` interp MEANS
    `the office on which the versions agree`
        (map (GIVEN v YIELD `Endnotes: the office that the definition of “Minister” names under the text of` v) (`Endnotes: the texts in force at some time on` `the day` interp))

@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Article 1, definition of “Minister”, as amended; Endnotes, Table of Legislation History (src:26), (src:876-912)
@export The office that the definition of “Minister” in Article 1 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 names at a given instant; refuses before 1 January 2019
GIVEN `the moment` IS A DATETIME @desc The moment asked about, with its time zone, for example 2024-02-27T09:29:59Z
      interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes` @desc The reading chosen at each fork; this function reads F7.2 and F7.11
GIVETH AN `Office of the Minister`
`Endnotes: the office of the Minister at` `the moment` interp MEANS
    `Endnotes: the office that the definition of “Minister” names under the text of` (`Endnotes: the vintage of the text at` `the moment` interp)

@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Article 1, definition of “Comptroller”, as amended; Endnotes, Table of Legislation History (src:12), (src:890-893)
@export The enactment that the definition of “Comptroller” in Article 1 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 points at on a given day; refuses before 1 January 2019
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day asked about, for example 2019-12-31
      interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes` @desc The reading chosen at each fork; this function reads F7.1
GIVETH AN `Enactment that defines the Comptroller`
`Endnotes: the enactment that defines the Comptroller on` `the day` interp MEANS
    `the enactment on which the versions agree`
        (map (GIVEN v YIELD `Endnotes: the enactment that defines the Comptroller under the text of` v) (`Endnotes: the texts in force at some time on` `the day` interp))

@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Article 1, definition of “Comptroller”, as amended; Endnotes, Table of Legislation History (src:12), (src:890-893)
@export The enactment that the definition of “Comptroller” in Article 1 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 points at at a given instant; refuses before 1 January 2019
GIVEN `the moment` IS A DATETIME @desc The moment asked about, with its time zone
      interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes` @desc The reading chosen at each fork; this function reads F7.2 and F7.11
GIVETH AN `Enactment that defines the Comptroller`
`Endnotes: the enactment that defines the Comptroller at` `the moment` interp MEANS
    `Endnotes: the enactment that defines the Comptroller under the text of` (`Endnotes: the vintage of the text at` `the moment` interp)

@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Article 2(1)(ba); Endnotes, Table of Legislation History, R&O.56/2025 (src:51-54), (src:907-909)
@export Whether paragraph (ba) of Article 2(1) of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 is in force on a given day; true from 16 October 2025; refuses before 1 January 2019
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day asked about, for example 2025-10-16
      interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes` @desc The reading chosen at each fork; this function reads F7.1
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Endnotes: Article 2(1)(ba) is in force on` `the day` interp MEANS
    `the answer on which the versions agree`
        (map (GIVEN v YIELD `Endnotes: Article 2(1)(ba) is in the text of` v) (`Endnotes: the texts in force at some time on` `the day` interp))

@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Article 2(1)(ba); Endnotes, Table of Legislation History, R&O.56/2025 (src:51-54), (src:907-909)
@export Whether paragraph (ba) of Article 2(1) of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 is in force at a given instant; refuses before 1 January 2019
GIVEN `the moment` IS A DATETIME @desc The moment asked about, with its time zone
      interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes` @desc The reading chosen at each fork; this function reads F7.2 and F7.11
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Endnotes: Article 2(1)(ba) is in force at` `the moment` interp MEANS
    `Endnotes: Article 2(1)(ba) is in the text of` (`Endnotes: the vintage of the text at` `the moment` interp)

@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Schedule 1 paragraphs 2(4)(a) and 4(7); Endnotes, Table of Legislation History, L.1/2017 (src:776), (src:806), (src:886-889)
@export Whether the two openings “subject to Article 20(1) of the Dormant Bank Accounts (Jersey) Law 2017” of Schedule 1 paragraphs 2(4)(a) and 4(7) of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 are in force on a given day; true from 16 December 2019; refuses before 1 January 2019
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day asked about, for example 2019-12-16
      interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes` @desc The reading chosen at each fork; this function reads F7.1
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Endnotes: the Dormant Bank Accounts openings of Schedule 1 are in force on` `the day` interp MEANS
    `the answer on which the versions agree`
        (map (GIVEN v YIELD `Endnotes: the Dormant Bank Accounts openings of Schedule 1 are in the text of` v) (`Endnotes: the texts in force at some time on` `the day` interp))

@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Schedule 1 paragraphs 2(4)(a) and 4(7); Endnotes, Table of Legislation History, L.1/2017 (src:776), (src:806), (src:886-889)
@export Whether the two openings “subject to Article 20(1) of the Dormant Bank Accounts (Jersey) Law 2017” of Schedule 1 are in force at a given instant; refuses before 1 January 2019
GIVEN `the moment` IS A DATETIME @desc The moment asked about, with its time zone
      interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes` @desc The reading chosen at each fork; this function reads F7.2 and F7.11
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Endnotes: the Dormant Bank Accounts openings of Schedule 1 are in force at` `the moment` interp MEANS
    `Endnotes: the Dormant Bank Accounts openings of Schedule 1 are in the text of` (`Endnotes: the vintage of the text at` `the moment` interp)

§§ `The amending instruments in force`

-- The amending instruments of the Table that are in force at an instant, and on a day.  (The Law itself, L.41/2014, and its Appointed Day Acts R&O.17/2018 and R&O.136/2019 are not amending
-- instruments of the Table: the commencement of the Law is in g7-commencement.)
@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Endnotes, Table of Legislation History (src:876-912)
@export The amending instruments of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 (the Table of Legislation History) that are in force at a given instant
GIVEN `the moment` IS A DATETIME @desc The moment asked about, with its time zone
      interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes` @desc The reading chosen at each fork; this function reads F7.2 and F7.11
GIVETH A LIST OF `Amending instrument`
`Endnotes: the amending instruments in force at` `the moment` interp MEANS
    mapMaybe (GIVEN row YIELD row's `brought by`)
             (filter (GIVEN row YIELD `the endnote instant` (`the instant at which a text of the Law takes effect` row interp) `is not later than the endnote instant` `the moment`)
                     `the nine texts of the Law`)

@ref Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Endnotes, Table of Legislation History (src:876-912)
@export The amending instruments of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 (the Table of Legislation History) that are in force on a given day; refuses on 27 February 2024 on the reading taken at F7.1 (R&O.10/2024 comes into force at 9.30 a.m.)
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day asked about, for example 2023-04-12
      interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes` @desc The reading chosen at each fork; this function reads F7.1, F7.2 and F7.11
GIVETH A LIST OF `Amending instrument`
`Endnotes: the amending instruments in force on` `the day` interp MEANS
    IF null (`the texts that take effect during` `the day` interp)
    THEN mapMaybe (GIVEN row YIELD row's `brought by`) (`the texts that have taken effect by the start of` `the day` interp)
    ELSE
        CONSIDER interp's `how a day on which a text takes effect at a stated time is treated`
        WHEN `a question about that day alone is refused` THEN `the text of the Law changes partway through this day, so a question about the day alone has no answer`
        WHEN `the whole day is in the new text` THEN
            mapMaybe (GIVEN row YIELD row's `brought by`)
                     (append (`the texts that have taken effect by the start of` `the day` interp) (`the texts that take effect during` `the day` interp))
